# Cloudflare Pages headers. Copied verbatim from public/ into the export root.
#
# Pages joins the values of a header set by more than one matching rule with
# a comma, and two comma-joined CSPs are both enforced. So each header below
# is defined once: security headers only in the /* block, Content-Type and
# Cache-Control only on paths that don't overlap. X-Robots-Tag rules don't
# overlap on blokcapital.io; on a *.pages.dev host an RSC payload gets
# "noindex, noindex", which is still valid. HSTS is set on the Cloudflare
# zone, not here (SEC-08). Every line stays under Pages' 2,000 characters.

# Hardening for every response (SEC-06, SEC-07; H §3.1, §3.2).
# - Permissions-Policy: lock off what the site never uses; the YouTube embed
#   (youtube-nocookie.com, D-26) keeps what its iframe `allow` asks for.
# - COOP same-origin: no window.open and every external link is noopener. If
#   an OAuth or wallet popup is ever added, use same-origin-allow-popups.
# - CSP is Report-Only for now (Stage 0 of H §3.2), so nothing can break
#   while it beds in; enforcing the same policy as Content-Security-Policy is
#   an owner step. Verified enforced, with 0 violations, across home, Accept
#   GA, /indices/blokc5, /token (live RPC read), /about + Play, /governance,
#   legal, the 404 and a client-side navigation. data: in img-src is for the
#   CSS mask images in globals.css. No upgrade-insecure-requests: browsers
#   ignore it in report-only mode and warn. Any new third party needs a CSP
#   change in the same PR.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=(), serial=(), hid=(), bluetooth=(), midi=(), display-capture=(), browsing-topics=(), accelerometer=(self "https://www.youtube-nocookie.com"), gyroscope=(self "https://www.youtube-nocookie.com"), autoplay=(self "https://www.youtube-nocookie.com"), encrypted-media=(self "https://www.youtube-nocookie.com"), picture-in-picture=(self "https://www.youtube-nocookie.com"), fullscreen=(self "https://www.youtube-nocookie.com"), clipboard-write=(self "https://www.youtube-nocookie.com"), web-share=(self "https://www.youtube-nocookie.com")
  Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://www.googletagmanager.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: https://*.google-analytics.com https://*.googletagmanager.com; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://arb1.arbitrum.io https://*.google-analytics.com https://*.analytics.google.com https://*.googletagmanager.com; frame-src https://www.youtube-nocookie.com; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'

# Preview and *.pages.dev aliases serve real builds (including unreleased
# branches); keep them out of search (SEO-06). The production domain has
# its own host, so these never match blokcapital.io.
https://:project.pages.dev/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
https://:version.:project.pages.dev/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex

# RFC 9116 security.txt (SEC-14). A dot-directory: check after deploy that
# Pages serves it.
/.well-known/security.txt
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8

# The social cards are exported as extensionless files (`/opengraph-image`
# and one per section), so Pages cannot infer their type and would serve
# application/octet-stream. Twitter and Facebook crawlers reject that, which
# silently kills link previews. Every opengraph-image.tsx needs a line here.
/opengraph-image
  Content-Type: image/png
/indices/:id/opengraph-image
  Content-Type: image/png
/token/opengraph-image
  Content-Type: image/png
/security/opengraph-image
  Content-Type: image/png
/protocol/opengraph-image
  Content-Type: image/png

# The static export's RSC payloads: one .txt per page with its full text,
# fetched by client-side navigation. Not documents to index or cite (SEO-19).
# Listed one by one so /llms.txt, /llms-full.txt, /robots.txt and
# /.well-known/security.txt stay indexable. Add a line for each new page.
# Cache stays on the Pages default, like the HTML (PERF-11).
/index.txt
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
/about.txt
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
/protocol.txt
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
/indices.txt
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
/indices/blokc2.txt
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
/indices/blokc5.txt
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
/indices/blokc10.txt
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
/security.txt
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
/token.txt
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
/governance.txt
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
/contact.txt
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
/legal/cookie-policy.txt
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
/legal/acceptable-use.txt
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
/legal/user-agreement.txt
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex

# Content-addressed by the build — safe to cache forever.
/_next/static/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Brand art. Not content-hashed, so a change needs a filename change (the
# renders are versioned by name: garden-01.webp, garden-02.webp, …).
/gardens/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/brand/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/teamgrid/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/textures/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/Socialtrust/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
# Token logos, on almost every page (PERF-11). Same rule: rename on change.
/tokens/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
